#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:5
msgid "AMDGPU Execution Synchronization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:12
msgid ""
"This document covers different ways of synchronizing execution of threads on "
"AMD GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:16
msgid ""
"This document is not exhaustive. There may be more ways of synchronizing "
"execution that are not covered by this document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:20
msgid "Barriers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:22
msgid ""
"This section covers execution synchronization using barrier-style primitives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:27
msgid "Execution Model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:29
msgid ""
"This section contains a formal execution model that can be used to model the "
"behavior of barriers on AMDGPU targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:34
msgid "The barrier execution model is experimental and subject to change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:36
msgid ""
"Threads can synchronize execution by performing barrier operations on "
"barrier *objects* as described below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:38
msgid "Each barrier *object* has the following state:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:40
msgid ""
"An unsigned positive integer *expected count*: counts the number of *arrive* "
"operations expected for this barrier *object*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:42
msgid ""
"An unsigned non-negative integer *arrive count*: counts the number of "
"*arrive* operations already performed on this barrier *object*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:45
msgid "The initial value of *arrive count* is zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:46
msgid ""
"When an operation causes *arrive count* to be equal to *expected count*, the "
"barrier is completed, and the *arrive count* is reset to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:49
msgid ""
"Barrier *objects* exist within a *scope* (see :ref:`amdgpu-amdhsa-llvm-sync-"
"scopes-table`), and each instance of a barrier *object* can only be accessed "
"by threads in the same *scope* instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:51
msgid ""
"*Barrier-mutually-exclusive* is a symmetric relation between barrier "
"*objects* that share resources in a way that restricts how a thread can use "
"them at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:53
msgid ""
"Barrier operations are performed on barrier *objects*. A barrier operation "
"is a dynamic instance of one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:56
msgid "Barrier *init*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:58
msgid ""
"Barrier *init* takes an additional unsigned positive integer argument *k*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:59
msgid "Sets the *expected count* of the *barrier object* to *k*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:60
msgid "Resets the *arrive count* of the *barrier object* to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:62
msgid "Barrier *join*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:64
msgid ""
"Allow the thread that executes the operation to *wait* on a barrier *object*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:66
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:86
msgid "Barrier *drop*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:68
msgid "Decrements *expected count* of the barrier *object* by one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:70
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:87
msgid "Barrier *arrive*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:72
msgid "Increments the *arrive count* of the barrier *object* by one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:73
msgid ""
"If supported, an additional argument to  *arrive* can also update the "
"*expected count* of the barrier *object* before the *arrive count* is "
"incremented; the new *expected count* cannot be less than or equal to the "
"*arrive count*, otherwise the behavior is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:78
msgid "Barrier *wait*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:80
msgid ""
"Introduces execution dependencies between threads; this operation depends on "
"other barrier operations to complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:83
msgid ""
"Barrier modification operations are barrier operations that modify the "
"barrier *object* state:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:85
msgid "Barrier *init*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:89
msgid ""
"*Thread-barrier-order<BO>* is the subset of *program-order* that only "
"relates barrier operations performed on a barrier *object* ``BO``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:91
msgid ""
"All barrier modification operations on a barrier *object* ``BO`` occur in a "
"strict total order called *barrier-modification-order<BO>*; it is the order "
"in which ``BO`` observes barrier operations that change its state. For any "
"valid *barrier-modification-order<BO>*, the following must be true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:96
msgid ""
"Let ``A`` and ``B`` be two barrier modification operations where ``A -> B`` "
"in *thread-barrier-order<BO>*, then ``A -> B`` is also in *barrier-"
"modification-order<BO>*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:98
msgid ""
"The first element in *barrier-modification-order<BO>* is always a barrier "
"*init*, otherwise the behavior is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:101
msgid ""
"*barrier-participates-in* relates barrier operations to the barrier *waits* "
"that depend on them to complete. A barrier operation ``X`` *barrier-"
"participates-in* a barrier *wait* ``W`` if and only if all of the following "
"is true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:105
msgid "``X`` and ``W`` are both performed on the same barrier *object* ``BO``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:106
msgid "``X`` is a barrier *arrive* or *drop* operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:107
msgid ""
"``X`` does not *barrier-participate-in* another distinct barrier *wait* "
"``W'`` in the same thread as ``W``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:108
msgid "``W -> X`` not in *thread-barrier-order<BO>*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:109
msgid "All dependent constraint and relations are satisfied as well. [0]_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:111
msgid ""
"For the set ``S`` consisting of all barrier operations that *barrier-"
"participate-in* a barrier *wait* ``W`` for some barrier *object* ``BO``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:114
msgid ""
"The elements of ``S`` all exist in a continuous, uninterrupted interval of "
"*barrier-modification-order<BO>*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:115
msgid ""
"The *arrive count* of ``BO`` is zero before the first operation of ``S`` in "
"*barrier-modification-order<BO>*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:116
msgid ""
"The *arrive count* and *expected count* of ``BO`` are equal after the last "
"operation of ``S`` in *barrier-modification-order<BO>*. The *arrive count* "
"and *expected count* of ``BO`` cannot equal at any other point in ``S``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:120
msgid ""
"A barrier *join* ``J`` is *barrier-joined-before* a barrier operation ``X`` "
"if and only if all of the following is true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:123
msgid "``J -> X`` in *thread-barrier-order<BO>*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:124
msgid "``X`` is not a barrier *join*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:125
msgid ""
"There is no barrier *join* or *drop* ``JD`` where ``J -> JD -> X`` in "
"*thread-barrier-order<BO>*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:126
msgid ""
"There is no barrier *join* ``J'`` on a distinct barrier *object* ``BO'`` "
"such that ``J -> J' -> X`` in *program-order*, and ``BO`` *barrier-mutually-"
"exclusive* ``BO'``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:129
msgid ""
"A barrier operation ``A`` *barrier-executes-before* another barrier "
"operation ``B`` if any of the following is true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:132
msgid "``A -> B`` in *program-order*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:133
msgid "``A -> B`` in *barrier-participates-in*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:134
msgid ""
"``A`` *barrier-executes-before* some barrier operation ``X``, and ``X`` "
"*barrier-executes-before* ``B``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:137
msgid ""
"*Barrier-executes-before* is consistent with *barrier-modification-"
"order<BO>* for every barrier object ``BO``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:139
msgid "For every barrier *drop* ``D`` performed on a barrier *object* ``BO``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:141
msgid ""
"There is a barrier *join* ``J`` such that ``J -> D`` in *barrier-joined-"
"before*; otherwise, the behavior is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:143
msgid ""
"``D`` cannot cause the *expected count* of ``BO`` to become negative; "
"otherwise, the behavior is undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:145
msgid ""
"For every pair of barrier *arrive* ``A`` and barrier *drop* ``D`` performed "
"on a barrier *object* ``BO``, such that ``A -> D`` in *thread-barrier-"
"order<BO>*, one of the following must be true:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:148
msgid "``A`` does not *barrier-participates-in* any barrier *wait*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:149
msgid ""
"``A`` *barrier-participates-in* at least one barrier *wait* ``W`` such that  "
"``W -> D`` in *barrier-executes-before*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:152
msgid "For every barrier *wait* ``W`` performed on a barrier *object* ``BO``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:154
msgid ""
"There is a barrier *join* ``J`` such that ``J -> W`` in *barrier-joined-"
"before*, and ``J`` must *barrier-executes-before* at least one operation "
"``X`` that *barrier-participates-in* ``W``; otherwise, the behavior is "
"undefined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:158
msgid ""
"*barrier-phase-with* is a symmetric relation over barrier operations defined "
"as the transitive closure of: *barrier-participates-in* and its inverse "
"relation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:160
msgid ""
"For every barrier operation ``A`` that *barrier-participates-in* a barrier "
"*wait* ``W`` on a barrier *object* ``BO``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:162
msgid ""
"There is no barrier operation ``X`` on ``BO`` such that ``A -> X -> W`` in "
"*barrier-executes-before*, and ``X`` *barrier-phase-with* a non-empty set of "
"operations that does not include ``W``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:168
msgid ""
"Barriers only synchronize execution and do not affect the visibility of "
"memory operations between threads. Refer to the :ref:`execution barriers "
"memory model<amdgpu-amdhsa-execution-barriers-memory-model>` to determine "
"how to synchronize memory operations through *barrier-executes-before*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:173
msgid ""
"The definition of *barrier-participates-in* (in its current state) is non-"
"deterministic and will be improved in the future: Within a valid execution, "
"there may be multiple ways to build *barrier-participates-in*, however there "
"is only one way to build it that also satisfies all other relations and "
"constraints that depend on *barrier-participates-in* and relations derived "
"from it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:179
msgid "Informational Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:181
msgid ""
"Informally, we can deduce from the above formal model that execution "
"barriers behave as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:183
msgid ""
"*Barrier-executes-before* relates the dynamic instances of operations from "
"different threads together. For example, if ``A -> B`` in *barrier-executes-"
"before*, then the execution of ``A`` must complete before the execution of "
"``B`` can complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:187
msgid ""
"This property can also be combined with *program-order*. For example, let "
"two (non-barrier) operations ``X`` and ``Y`` where ``X -> A`` and ``B -> Y`` "
"in *program-order*, then we know that the execution of ``X`` completes "
"before the execution of ``Y`` does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:191
msgid ""
"Barriers do not complete \"out-of-thin-air\"; a barrier *wait* ``W`` cannot "
"depend on a barrier operation ``X`` to complete if ``W -> X`` in *barrier-"
"executes-before*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:193
msgid "It is undefined behavior to operate on an uninitialized barrier object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:194
msgid "It is undefined behavior for a barrier *wait* to never complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:195
msgid "It is not mandatory to *drop* a barrier after *joining* it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:196
msgid ""
"A thread may not *arrive* and then *drop* a barrier *object* unless the "
"barrier completes before the barrier *drop*. Incrementing the *arrive count* "
"and decrementing the *expected count* directly after may cause undefined "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:199
msgid ""
"*Joining* a barrier is only useful if the thread will *wait* on that same "
"barrier *object* later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:202
msgid "Barrier Implementations on AMDGPU Targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:0
#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:205
msgid "``s_barrier``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:207
msgid "``s_barrier`` are the primary barrier implementation of AMD GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:209
msgid ""
"``s_barrier`` instructions can only be used to synchronize threads at a "
"wavefront granularity. ``s_barrier`` instructions are convergent within a "
"wave, and thus can only be performed in wave-uniform control flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:213
msgid ""
"The ``s_barrier`` family of instructions is available in some form on all "
"GFX targets, and has evolved over time. The sub-sections below cover the "
"capabilities offered by every major iteration of this feature separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:218
msgid "GFX6-11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:220
msgid ""
"Targets from GFX6 through GFX11 included do not have the \"split barrier\" "
"feature. The barrier *arrive* and barrier *wait* operations **cannot** be "
"performed independently using ``s_barrier``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUExecutionSynchronization.rst:224
msgid ""
"There is only one *workgroup barrier* object of ``workgroup`` scope that is "
"implicitly used by all ``s_barrier`` instructions."
msgstr ""

